# Deny-list on purpose.
#
# This used to be an allow-list -- `**` to drop everything, then `!**/*.go` to
# bring the sources back. That only works under BuildKit. The classic builder
# does not descend into a directory it has already excluded, so the re-include
# never reaches cmd/main.go, and the build fails with the unhelpful
# "package cmd/main.go is not in std" -- go's way of saying the file is absent.
# Verified by building this context with DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0: go.mod arrived and
# nothing else. The internal pipeline runs the classic builder deliberately, so
# the ignore file has to work for both.
.git
.github
.devcontainer
.githooks
bin
dist
docs
test
*.md
*.svg
